Publish the personalities of the statically linked NioUfs driver

NioUfs is linked into this kernel as a static archive: no kext bundle, no
prelink record, no OSKext object.  Nothing reads the IOKitPersonalities in
its Info.plist, so no personality ever reaches gIOCatalogue.  Its
constructor prints "nio: ufs driver is linked in", but probe()/start() are
never called -- no provider is offered to a personality that does not
exist.  The result is the boot's last wall: no IOMedia with the OS volume
UUID is published, waitForService() times out, and IOService panics
"Failed to mount root device" @IOKitBSDInit.cpp.

The matching sweep starts at startIOServiceMatching() below and reads the
catalogue at that moment.  Publish the two personalities just before it:
one attaches to the platform expert (root device), one to the UFS
controller nub.  The official xnu-10063 OS series carries no such patch,
which is why the problem came back when the board moved to the official
iPadOS 17.7.11 chain.

Against xnu-10063.141.1 (d8b8029), iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
index d74c063..7a2f723 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/IOStartIOKit.cpp
@@ -182,6 +182,42 @@ StartIOKitMatching(void)
 {
 	SOCD_TRACE_XNU(START_IOKIT);
 	assert(gRootNub != NULL);
+	/*
+	 * nio: publish the personalities of the board drivers that are linked
+	 * into this kernel as static archives.  A static archive has no bundle
+	 * and no OSKext object, so its Info.plist is never read and its
+	 * personalities never reach the catalogue the matcher reads.  Add them
+	 * here, immediately before the matching sweep starts.
+	 */
+	{
+		OSArray      *personalities = OSArray::withCapacity(2);
+		OSDictionary *storage       = OSDictionary::withCapacity(4);
+		OSDictionary *storageRoot   = OSDictionary::withCapacity(4);
+		OSString     *classStorage  = OSString::withCString("NioUfs");
+		OSString     *providerExpert = OSString::withCString("IOPlatformExpertDevice");
+		OSString     *providerDevice = OSString::withCString("IOPlatformDevice");
+		OSNumber     *scoreStorage   = OSNumber::withNumber(1000, 32);
+		OSNumber     *scoreRoot      = OSNumber::withNumber(500, 32);
+
+		if (personalities && storage && storageRoot && classStorage &&
+		    providerExpert && providerDevice && scoreStorage && scoreRoot) {
+			storage->setObject("IOClass", classStorage);
+			storage->setObject("IOProviderClass", providerDevice);
+			storage->setObject("IOProbeScore", scoreStorage);
+			personalities->setObject(storage);
+
+			storageRoot->setObject("IOClass", classStorage);
+			storageRoot->setObject("IOProviderClass", providerExpert);
+			storageRoot->setObject("IOProbeScore", scoreRoot);
+			personalities->setObject(storageRoot);
+
+			printf("\nnio: publishing %d static personalities",
+			       (int) personalities->getCount());
+			gIOCatalogue->addDrivers(personalities, false);
+		}
+
+		printf("\nnio: static personalities published before match");
+	}
 	bool ok = gRootNub->startIOServiceMatching();
 	if (__improbable(!ok)) {
 		panic("Failed to start IOService matching");
